        "notes": "Click into this formula after n= (e.g. double[mod.map()](wf[\"readings\"], n=)), then pick in readings' grid. Each pick is written at the caret in core's notation and the next pick replaces it (as in Excel): a cell -> wf[\"readings\"][0][cols[\"n\"]] (row id); Shift-click or drag to a block -> wf[\"readings\"][0:2][cols[\"n\"]] (positions); a column header -> wf[\"readings\"][cols[\"n\"]]; Cmd/Ctrl-click rows -> wf[\"readings\"][[0, 2]]; the corner -> wf[\"readings\"]. The pick is the bold outline in readings' grid; no select step is added, and the window never opens while picking. Scattered cells that aren't one rectangle write nothing. Still to come: dashed reference boxes in the bar and the grid (R3)."
      }
